[size=4][b][color=#C0860A]I[/color][color=#CA9623]n[/color][color=#D4A63B]s[/color][color=#DDB654]t[/color][color=#E7C66D]a[/color][color=#F1D686]l[/color][color=#F1D686]l[/color][color=#E7C66D]a[/color][color=#DDB654]t[/color][color=#D4A63B]i[/color][color=#CA9623]o[/color][color=#C0860A]n[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Option 1 - [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]Mod Engine 2[/url] (recommended)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Mod Engine 2 from the link above and extract it into your game folder (the same folder as [i]eldenring.exe[/i]).[/*]
[*]Download this mod, then create a folder to hold it and its INI file - for example, inside your game folder create a [b]natives[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Open [b]config_eldenring.toml[/b] and edit [b]external_dlls = [ ][/b] to add the DLL, e.g.:
[code]external_dlls = [
    "natives\\RiseArcher.dll",
][/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch the game using Mod Engine 2's launcher, [b]modengine2_launcher.exe[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[b]Option 2 - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Elden Mod Loader from the link above and extract it into your game folder.[/*]
[*]Download this mod and drag [b]RiseArcher.dll[/b] and [b]RiseArcher.ini[/b] into the [b]mods[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game - the mod will be loaded automatically.[/*]
[/list]

Because the DLL doesn't touch [b]regulation.bin[/b] at all, it's compatible with any other regulation.bin-editing mod - no merging with Smithbox required.

[spoiler]Prefer editing regulation.bin directly instead of running a DLL? The same changes are also available as a Smithbox Mass Edit / CSV import, exactly like the original release of this mod.

[b]Option 1 - Mass Edit[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://github.com/vawser/Smithbox]Smithbox[/url] and open your regulation.bin as a project, then go to [b]Param Editor[/b].[/*]
[*]Download [b]RiseArcher.MASSEDIT[/b] from this mod's files and open it in a text editor.[/*]
[*]In the right-hand panel, click [b]Mass Edit[/b], then open the [b]Command Palette[/b] tab.[/*]
[*]Copy the entire contents of [b]RiseArcher.MASSEDIT[/b], paste it into the input box, and click [b]Apply[/b].[/*]
[*]Save the project - you can now copy the resulting regulation.bin wherever you need it.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Option 2 - CSV import[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install Smithbox and open your regulation.bin as a project, then go to [b]Param Editor[/b].[/*]
[*]Download [b]EquipParamWeapon.csv[/b] and [b]Bullet.csv[/b] from this mod's files.[/*]
[*]In the param list, find and click on [b]Bullet[/b], then in the top menu go to [b]Tools > Data Transfer > Import CSV > From File > All Fields[/b] and select [b]Bullet.csv[/b].[/*]
[*]Do the same for [b]EquipParamWeapon[/b], selecting [b]EquipParamWeapon.csv[/b] this time.[/*]
[*]Save the project, then copy the resulting regulation.bin into your game folder or your Mod Engine 2 mod folder.[/*]
[/list]
Note: CSV import overwrites entire rows with the values from the file, so it will discard any other mod's changes to the same rows - use Option 1 (Mass Edit) if you need to preserve those.

This static regulation.bin file - unlike the DLL - does conflict with other mods that also edit regulation.bin. Merge it with Smithbox as shown above rather than installing both.
[/spoiler]

